{"Cluster_ZNF446_4": [{"paragraph": "*RAE1, NOL3, RANBP3*, and *NXF1-like pathways* are involved in **mRNA export and nuclear-cytoplasmic trafficking**. These genes facilitate mature transcript movement from the nucleus to the cytoplasm, often in conjunction with exon-junction complex (EJC)-associated surveillance. ", "keyword": "(\"RAE1\" OR \"NOL3\" OR \"RANBP3\") AND (\"mRNA export\" OR \"nuclear-cytoplasmic trafficking\" OR \"exon-junction complex\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Satterly, Neal, Tsai, Pei-Ling, van Deursen, Jan, Nussenzveig, Daniel R, Wang, Yaming, Faria, Paula A, Levay, Agata, Levy, David E, Fontoura, Beatriz M A. \"Influenza virus targets the mRNA export machinery and the nuclear pore complex.\" Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America, 2007, pp. 1853-8, doi: https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0610977104", "Faria, Paula A, Chakraborty, Papia, Levay, Agata, Barber, Glen N, Ezelle, Heather J, Enninga, Jost, Arana, Carlos, van Deursen, Jan, Fontoura, Beatriz M A. \"VSV disrupts the Rae1/mrnp41 mRNA nuclear export pathway.\" Molecular cell, 2005, pp. 93-102, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molcel.2004.11.023", "Pritchard, C E, Fornerod, M, Kasper, L H, van Deursen, J M. \"RAE1 is a shuttling mRNA export factor that binds to a GLEBS-like NUP98 motif at the nuclear pore complex through multiple domains.\" The Journal of cell biology, 1999, pp. 237-54, doi: https://doi.org/10.1083/jcb.145.2.237"]}], "Cluster_ZNF446_5": [{"paragraph": "Several components like *USP19, UBOX5, STUB1, FBXW4, RNF31, TRIM46, TRIM68* reflect a system for **deubiquitylation, ubiquitin ligation, and proteostasis** for RNA-associated or misfolded proteins. Their presence supports a coordinated **quality control system for RNA-protein complexes**, especially during co-transcriptional and co-translational surveillance. ", "keyword": "(\"USP19\" OR \"UBOX5\" OR \"STUB1\" OR \"FBXW4\" OR \"RNF31\" OR \"TRIM46\" OR \"TRIM68\") AND (\"deubiquitylation\" OR \"proteostasis\" OR \"quality control\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Liu, Yongshuo, Zhou, Honghong, Tang, Xiaolong. \"STUB1/CHIP: New insights in cancer and immunity.\" Biomedicine & pharmacotherapy = Biomedecine & pharmacotherapie, 2023, pp. 115190, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopha.2023.115190", "Sarodaya, Neha, Tyagi, Apoorvi, Kim, Hyun-Jin, Colaco, Jencia Carminha, Kang, Ju-Seop, Kim, Woo Jin, Kim, Kye-Seong, Ramakrishna, Suresh. \"Deubiquitinase USP19 enhances phenylalanine hydroxylase protein stability and its enzymatic activity.\" Cell biology and toxicology, 2023, pp. 2295-2310, doi: https://doi.org/10.1007/s10565-022-09719-z"]}], "Cluster_ZNF446_6": [{"paragraph": "*ZNF646, ZNF263, MED29, E4F1* and *PIAS3* influence transcriptional dynamics via **chromatin structure modulation and SUMOylation-related transcriptional silencing or activation**. These genes mediate fine control of RNA polymerase access and transcription factor recruitment. ", "keyword": "(\"ZNF646\" OR \"ZNF263\" OR \"MED29\" OR \"E4F1\" OR \"PIAS3\") AND (\"chromatin\" OR \"SUMOylation\" OR \"transcription\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": []}], "Cluster_ZC3H4_1": [{"paragraph": "This system is centered around a dense cluster of **RNA-binding proteins (RBPs)** such as *ILF3, PTBP1, HNRNPL, HNRNPA3, HNRNPD, HNRNPM, HNRNPR, HNRNPH3, HNRNPUL1, SFPQ, SYNCRIP, KHSRP, KHDRBS1, DAZAP1, SF1, SF3A1, SF3A2, SF3B2, SF3B3, SRSF9, SRSF10*, and *U2AF2*. These proteins function in **splice site recognition, alternative splicing regulation, exon definition, and RNA stabilization**, often in a co-transcriptional manner. Their interactions modulate splicing outcomes and determine transcript isoform diversity. ", "keyword": "(\"ILF3\" OR \"PTBP1\" OR \"HNRNPL\" OR \"HNRNPA3\" OR \"HNRNPD\" OR \"HNRNPM\" OR \"HNRNPR\" OR \"HNRNPH3\" OR \"HNRNPUL1\" OR \"SFPQ\" OR \"SYNCRIP\" OR \"KHSRP\" OR \"KHDRBS1\" OR \"DAZAP1\" OR \"SF1\" OR \"SF3A1\" OR \"SF3A2\" OR \"SF3B2\" OR \"SF3B3\" OR \"SRSF9\" OR \"SRSF10\" OR \"U2AF2\") AND (\"RNA-binding\" OR \"splicing\" OR \"transcript isoform diversity\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Shkreta, Lulzim, Delannoy, Aur\u00e9lie, Salvetti, Anna, Chabot, Benoit. \"SRSF10: an atypical splicing regulator with critical roles in stress response, organ development, and viral replication.\" RNA (New York, N.Y.), 2021, pp. 1302-1317, doi: https://doi.org/10.1261/rna.078879.121", "Ye, Rong, Hu, Naijing, Cao, Changchang, Su, Ruibao, Xu, Shihan, Yang, Chen, Zhou, Xiangtian, Xue, Yuanchao. \"Capture RIC-seq reveals positional rules of PTBP1-associated RNA loops in splicing regulation.\" Molecular cell, 2023, pp. 1311-1327.e7, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molcel.2023.03.001", "Lim, Yee Wa, James, Dylan, Huang, Jie, Lee, Mihwa. \"The Emerging Role of the RNA-Binding Protein SFPQ in Neuronal Function and Neurodegeneration.\" International journal of molecular sciences, 2020, pp.  , doi: https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms21197151"]}], "Cluster_ZC3H4_2": [{"paragraph": "The system includes multiple **transcription-associated co-regulators and chromatin remodelers** such as *TAF4, GTF2F1, POLR3B, CARM1, TRIM28, SMARCA4, SMARCC1, ARID1A, BRPF1, EP300, MTA1, MTA2, MED12, MED22, MED25*, and *TRRAP*. These factors support **transcription initiation, elongation, and histone modification**, providing a molecular scaffold that connects **RNA synthesis to downstream splicing and RBP activity**. *CTCF* and *SAFB/SAFB2* contribute to RNA-chromatin tethering and nuclear organization, further supporting regulated transcript output at the chromatin level. ", "keyword": "(\"TAF4\" OR \"GTF2F1\" OR \"POLR3B\" OR \"CARM1\" OR \"TRIM28\" OR \"SMARCA4\" OR \"SMARCC1\" OR \"ARID1A\" OR \"BRPF1\" OR \"EP300\" OR \"MTA1\" OR \"MTA2\" OR \"MED12\" OR \"MED22\" OR \"MED25\" OR \"TRRAP\" OR \"CTCF\" OR \"SAFB\" OR \"SAFB2\") AND (\"transcription\" OR \"chromatin\" OR \"splicing\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Bakr, Ali, Della Corte, Giuditta, Veselinov, Olivera, Kelek\u00e7i, Simge, Chen, Mei-Ju May, Lin, Yu-Yu, Sigismondo, Gianluca, Iacovone, Marika, Cross, Alice, Syed, Rabail, Jeong, Yunhee, Sollier, Etienne, Liu, Chun-Shan, Lutsik, Pavlo, Krijgsveld, Jeroen, Weichenhan, Dieter, Plass, Christoph, Popanda, Odilia, Schmezer, Peter. \"ARID1A regulates DNA repair through chromatin organization and its deficiency triggers DNA damage-mediated anti-tumor immune response.\" Nucleic acids research, 2024, pp. 5698-5719, doi: https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkae233"]}], "Cluster_ZC3H4_3": [{"paragraph": "Core spliceosomal proteins such as *PRPF31, PRPF19, DDX23, DDX46, SART1, SART3, SUPT5H, SUPT6H, SSRP1, NELFB, NELFA* form the **molecular machinery for spliceosome formation and dynamics**, including exon junction complex (EJC) recruitment and coupling to mRNA export readiness. Splicing co-factors like *SUGP1, PAF1, POLDIP3, SRRT*, and *RAVER1* coordinate spliceosomal transitions and post-splicing mRNP maturation. ", "keyword": "(\"PRPF31\" OR \"PRPF19\" OR \"DDX23\" OR \"DDX46\" OR \"SART1\" OR \"SART3\" OR \"SUPT5H\" OR \"SUPT6H\" OR \"SSRP1\" OR \"NELFB\" OR \"NELFA\" OR \"SUGP1\" OR \"PAF1\" OR \"POLDIP3\" OR \"SRRT\" OR \"RAVER1\") AND (\"spliceosome\" OR \"splicing\" OR \"mRNA export\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Rose, Anna M, Luo, Rong, Radia, Utsav K, Bhattacharya, Shomi S. \"Gene of the month: <i>PRPF31</i>.\" Journal of clinical pathology, 2017, pp. 729-732, doi: https://doi.org/10.1136/jclinpath-2016-203971", "Zhang, Yuzhe, Li, Yue, Liang, Xiao, Zhu, Zhongliang, Sun, Hongbin, He, Hao, Min, Jinrong, Liao, Shanhui, Liu, Yanli. \"Crystal structure of the WD40 domain of human PRPF19.\" Biochemical and biophysical research communications, 2017, pp. 1250-1253, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbrc.2017.09.145", "Segovia, Danilo, Adams, Dexter W, Hoffman, Nickolas, Safaric Tepes, Polona, Wee, Tse-Luen, Cifani, Paolo, Joshua-Tor, Leemor, Krainer, Adrian R. \"SRSF1 interactome determined by proximity labeling reveals direct interaction with spliceosomal RNA helicase DDX23.\" Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America, 2024, pp. e2322974121, doi: https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2322974121"]}], "Cluster_ZC3H4_4": [{"paragraph": "*RANBP3, NUP153, NUP214, UPF1, GEMIN6*, and *UBAP2L* participate in **mRNA nuclear export and surveillance**, coupling transcript processing with quality control and cytoplasmic export readiness. The presence of *SMG family members*, *TUT1*, and *ADAR* links this system to **RNA modification and degradation pathways**. ", "keyword": "(\"RANBP3\" OR \"NUP153\" OR \"NUP214\" OR \"UPF1\" OR \"GEMIN6\" OR \"UBAP2L\" OR \"TUT1\" OR \"ADAR\") AND (\"mRNA nuclear export\" OR \"RNA modification\" OR \"quality control\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Kurosaki, Tatsuaki, Maquat, Lynne E. \"Nonsense-mediated mRNA decay in humans at a glance.\" Journal of cell science, 2016, pp. 461-7, doi: https://doi.org/10.1242/jcs.181008", "Walkley, Carl R, Li, Jin Billy. \"Rewriting the transcriptome: adenosine-to-inosine RNA editing by ADARs.\" Genome biology, 2017, pp. 205, doi: https://doi.org/10.1186/s13059-017-1347-3", "Fritzell, Kajsa, Xu, Li-Di, Lagergren, Jens, \u00d6hman, Marie. \"ADARs and editing: The role of A-to-I RNA modification in cancer progression.\" Seminars in cell & developmental biology, 2018, pp. 123-130, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.semcdb.2017.11.018"]}], "Cluster_ZC3H4_5": [{"paragraph": "The system features numerous **epigenetic regulators**, including *KDM3B, KDM4A, KDM4D, EHMT2, MBD2, MBD3, MBD6, SETD1A, BRD1, BRD3, BRD8*, and *BAZ family members*. These functionally integrate **histone methylation and acetylation status with RNA Pol II recruitment and pre-mRNA processing**, influencing transcriptional elongation rate and exon inclusion. ", "keyword": "(\"KDM3B\" OR \"KDM4A\" OR \"KDM4D\" OR \"EHMT2\" OR \"MBD2\" OR \"MBD3\" OR \"MBD6\" OR \"SETD1A\" OR \"BRD1\" OR \"BRD3\" OR \"BRD8\") AND (\"epigenetic regulation\" OR \"transcription\" OR \"chromatin remodeling\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Guerra-Calderas, Lissania, Gonz\u00e1lez-Barrios, Rodrigo, Herrera, Luis A, Cant\u00fa de Le\u00f3n, David, Soto-Reyes, Ernesto. \"The role of the histone demethylase KDM4A in cancer.\" Cancer genetics, 2015, pp. 215-24, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cancergen.2014.11.001"]}], "Cluster_ZC3H4_6": [{"paragraph": "Enzymes such as *TUT1, TRMT1L, METTL13, ADAT1, ADAT3*, and *ZC3H7B* contribute to **RNA editing, methylation, and uridylation**, modulating mRNA half-life and translation efficiency. These post-transcriptional marks influence RBP binding and splicing outcomes. ", "keyword": "(\"TUT1\" OR \"TRMT1L\" OR \"METTL13\" OR \"ADAT1\" OR \"ADAT3\" OR \"ZC3H7B\") AND (\"RNA editing\" OR \"methylation\" OR \"uridylation\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Yamashita, Seisuke, Tomita, Kozo. \"Mechanism of U6 snRNA oligouridylation by human TUT1.\" Nature communications, 2023, pp. 4686, doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-40420-9"]}], "Cluster_ZC3H4_7": [{"paragraph": "*NOP14, FBL, NCL, RRS1*, and *UBTF* link **rRNA processing and ribonucleoprotein biogenesis** with RNA-binding activity, suggesting that nuclear pre-mRNA and rRNA processing are coordinated in shared subcompartments (e.g., nucleoli). ", "keyword": "(\"NOP14\" OR \"FBL\" OR \"NCL\" OR \"RRS1\" OR \"UBTF\") AND (\"rRNA processing\" OR \"ribonucleoprotein biogenesis\" OR \"RNA-binding activity\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Yao, Run-Wen, Xu, Guang, Wang, Ying, Shan, Lin, Luan, Peng-Fei, Wang, Yang, Wu, Man, Yang, Liang-Zhong, Xing, Yu-Hang, Yang, Li, Chen, Ling-Ling. \"Nascent Pre-rRNA Sorting via Phase Separation Drives the Assembly of Dense Fibrillar Components in the Human Nucleolus.\" Molecular cell, 2019, pp. 767-783.e11, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molcel.2019.08.014", "Ueshima, Shuhei, Nagata, Kyosuke, Okuwaki, Mitsuru. \"Upstream binding factor-dependent and pre-rRNA transcription-independent association of pre-rRNA processing factors with rRNA gene.\" Biochemical and biophysical research communications, 2014, pp. 22-7, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbrc.2013.11.039"]}], "Cluster_POLR2G_1": [{"paragraph": "This system includes a large number of **ribosomal protein genes** from both the small (RPS) and large (RPL) subunits\u2014*RPS3, RPS3A, RPS5, RPS7, RPS11, RPS12, RPS13, RPS14, RPS15A, RPS18, RPS21, RPS24, RPS25, RPS27, RPS27A, RPS29, RPL15, RPL21, RPL23, RPL23A, RPL24, RPL30, RPL34, RPL36A, RPL37A, RPL38, RPL39, RPL7A*. These proteins contribute to **ribosome structure and function**, including mRNA decoding, peptidyl transfer, and translational control. Their expression and incorporation are tightly coupled with **ribosome biogenesis**, requiring stoichiometric synthesis and nuclear processing before cytoplasmic translation assembly. ", "keyword": "(\"RPS3\" OR \"RPS3A\" OR \"RPS5\" OR \"RPS7\" OR \"RPS11\" OR \"RPS12\" OR \"RPS13\" OR \"RPS14\" OR \"RPS15A\" OR \"RPS18\" OR \"RPS21\" OR \"RPS24\" OR \"RPS25\" OR \"RPS27\" OR \"RPS27A\" OR \"RPS29\" OR \"RPL15\" OR \"RPL21\" OR \"RPL23\" OR \"RPL23A\" OR \"RPL24\" OR \"RPL30\" OR \"RPL34\" OR \"RPL36A\" OR \"RPL37A\" OR \"RPL38\" OR \"RPL39\" OR \"RPL7A\") AND (\"ribosome\" OR \"translation\" OR \"biogenesis\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Ebright, Richard Y, Lee, Sooncheol, Wittner, Ben S, Niederhoffer, Kira L, Nicholson, Benjamin T, Bardia, Aditya, Truesdell, Samuel, Wiley, Devon F, Wesley, Benjamin, Li, Selena, Mai, Andy, Aceto, Nicola, Vincent-Jordan, Nicole, Szabolcs, Annamaria, Chirn, Brian, Kreuzer, Johannes, Comaills, Valentine, Kalinich, Mark, Haas, Wilhelm, Ting, David T, Toner, Mehmet, Vasudevan, Shobha, Haber, Daniel A, Maheswaran, Shyamala, Micalizzi, Douglas S. \"Deregulation of ribosomal protein expression and translation promotes breast cancer metastasis.\" Science (New York, N.Y.), 2020, pp. 1468-1473, doi: https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aay0939", "Kubickova, Agata, Maceckova, Zuzana, Vojta, Petr, Ondra, Martin, Volejnikova, Jana, Koralkova, Pavla, Jungova, Alexandra, Jahoda, Ond\u0159ej, Mojzikova, Renata, Hadacova, Ivana, Cermak, Jaroslav, Horvathova, Monika, Pospisilova, Dagmar, Hajduch, Marian. \"Missense mutation in RPS7 causes Diamond-Blackfan anemia via alteration of erythrocyte metabolism, protein translation and induction of ribosomal stress.\" Blood cells, molecules & diseases, 2022, pp. 102690, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bcmd.2022.102690"]}], "Cluster_POLR2G_2": [{"paragraph": "Key components of **rRNA processing and small nucleolar ribonucleoprotein (snoRNP) complexes** include *NOP10*, *FCF1*, *EXOSC8*, and *CWF19L1*. These proteins contribute to **cleavage, trimming, and chemical modification** (e.g., pseudouridylation, methylation) of precursor rRNA within the nucleolus. *DCPS* is also involved in RNA turnover and decapping pathways. *METTL12* and *METTL6* act as **RNA methyltransferases**, potentially modifying tRNAs or small RNAs, influencing translational fidelity and ribonucleoprotein stability. ", "keyword": "(\"NOP10\" OR \"FCF1\" OR \"EXOSC8\" OR \"CWF19L1\" OR \"DCPS\" OR \"CSKMT\" OR \"METTL6\") AND (\"rRNA processing\" OR \"RNA methylation\" OR \"snoRNP complexes\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Walne, Amanda J, Vulliamy, Tom, Marrone, Anna, Beswick, Richard, Kirwan, Michael, Masunari, Yuka, Al-Qurashi, Fat-Hia, Aljurf, Mahmoud, Dokal, Inderjeet. \"Genetic heterogeneity in autosomal recessive dyskeratosis congenita with one subtype due to mutations in the telomerase-associated protein NOP10.\" Human molecular genetics, 2007, pp. 1619-29, doi: https://doi.org/10.1093/hmg/ddm111", "Khanna, May, Wu, Haihong, Johansson, Carina, Caizergues-Ferrer, Mich\u00e8le, Feigon, Juli. \"Structural study of the H/ACA snoRNP components Nop10p and the 3' hairpin of U65 snoRNA.\" RNA (New York, N.Y.), 2006, pp. 40-52, doi: https://doi.org/10.1261/rna.2221606", "Li, Shibiao, Zhou, Hualin, Liao, Shanhui, Wang, Xiaoyang, Zhu, Zhongliang, Zhang, Jiahai, Xu, Chao. \"Structural basis for METTL6-mediated m3C RNA methylation.\" Biochemical and biophysical research communications, 2022, pp. 159-164, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbrc.2021.12.013"]}], "Cluster_POLR2G_3": [{"paragraph": "Translational machinery components such as *EIF4E2* (eukaryotic translation initiation factor) and *TXNL4B* contribute to **initiation complex formation**, ribosome recruitment, and re-initiation. *GEMIN2* and *WIBG* (a.k.a. PYM1) assist in **exon junction complex recycling** and link mRNA export to translation readiness. *SUPT4H1* integrates with the transcription-translation interface, ensuring **transcript stability and export coordination** for translational activation. ", "keyword": "(\"EIF4E2\" OR \"TXNL4B\" OR \"GEMIN2\" OR \"PYM1\" OR \"SUPT4H1\") AND (\"translation\" OR \"initiation\" OR \"transcript\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Melanson, Gaelan, Timpano, Sara, Uniacke, James. \"The eIF4E2-Directed Hypoxic Cap-Dependent Translation Machinery Reveals Novel Therapeutic Potential for Cancer Treatment.\" Oxidative medicine and cellular longevity, 2017, pp. 6098107, doi: https://doi.org/10.1155/2017/6098107"]}], "Cluster_POLR2G_4": [{"paragraph": "The presence of *PSMD9, PSMD10, PSMB8, PSMB10, PSME1* indicates **proteasomal degradation components** involved in **ribosome-associated quality control (RQC)** and clearance of stalled nascent peptide chains. RQC components are critical for maintaining fidelity during translation and surveilling defective ribosomes or misfolded nascent proteins. ", "keyword": "(\"PSMD9\" OR \"PSMD10\" OR \"PSMB8\" OR \"PSMB10\" OR \"PSME1\") AND (\"proteasomal degradation\" OR \"quality control\" OR \"translation fidelity\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": []}], "Cluster_POLR2G_5": [{"paragraph": "*NUP133*, *RPAIN*, and *ZMAT2* regulate **nuclear-cytoplasmic export of mRNAs and ribonucleoprotein complexes**. *SIRT3, HDAC1, KAT5*, and *CHD family members* contribute to **chromatin remodeling and transcriptional activity** affecting rRNA gene expression. *BCDIN3D* and *RBM3* support RNA stability and export readiness, ensuring processed RNAs reach translationally competent cytoplasmic ribosomes. ", "keyword": "(\"NUP133\" OR \"RPAIN\" OR \"ZMAT2\" OR \"SIRT3\" OR \"HDAC1\" OR \"KAT5\" OR \"BCDIN3D\" OR \"RBM3\") AND (\"nuclear-cytoplasmic export\" OR \"chromatin remodeling\" OR \"RNA stability\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": []}], "Cluster_RPLP0_1": [{"paragraph": "This system contains a defined subset of **cytosolic ribosomal proteins**, including *RPL10, RPL31, RPL32, RPL37A, RPL39, RPS9, RPS19*, supporting **ribosome biogenesis and protein synthesis**. These proteins contribute to ribosome stability, peptidyl transferase activity, and translational elongation. Their consistent presence indicates active **translational output and regulation**. ", "keyword": "(\"RPL10\" OR \"RPL31\" OR \"RPL32\" OR \"RPL37A\" OR \"RPL39\" OR \"RPS9\" OR \"RPS19\") AND (\"ribosome biogenesis\" OR \"protein synthesis\" OR \"translational regulation\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["De Keersmaecker, Kim, Atak, Zeynep Kalender, Li, Ning, Vicente, Carmen, Patchett, Stephanie, Girardi, Tiziana, Gianfelici, Valentina, Geerdens, Ellen, Clappier, Emmanuelle, Porcu, Micha\u00ebl, Lahortiga, Idoya, Luc\u00e0, Rossella, Yan, Jiekun, Hulselmans, Gert, Vranckx, Hilde, Vandepoel, Roel, Sweron, Bram, Jacobs, Kris, Mentens, Nicole, Wlodarska, Iwona, Cauwelier, Barbara, Cloos, Jacqueline, Soulier, Jean, Uyttebroeck, Anne, Bagni, Claudia, Hassan, Bassem A, Vandenberghe, Peter, Johnson, Arlen W, Aerts, Stein, Cools, Jan. \"Exome sequencing identifies mutation in CNOT3 and ribosomal genes RPL5 and RPL10 in T-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia.\" Nature genetics, 2013, pp. 186-90, doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.2508", "L\u00e9ger-Silvestre, Isabelle, Caffrey, Jacqueline Marie, Dawaliby, Rosy, Alvarez-Arias, Diana Alehandrovna, Gas, Nicole, Bertolone, Salvatore J, Gleizes, Pierre-Emmanuel, Ellis, Steven Robert. \"Specific Role for Yeast Homologs of the Diamond Blackfan Anemia-associated Rps19 Protein in Ribosome Synthesis.\" The Journal of biological chemistry, 2005, pp. 38177-85, doi: https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M506916200", "Pollutri, Daniela, Penzo, Marianna. \"Ribosomal Protein L10: From Function to Dysfunction.\" Cells, 2020, pp.  , doi: https://doi.org/10.3390/cells9112503"]}], "Cluster_RPLP0_2": [{"paragraph": "*SCARNA12* and *SNORA68* are **small Cajal body- and nucleolar RNAs**, respectively, that guide site-specific **modifications (pseudouridylation and 2'-O-methylation)** of rRNA and snRNA. These modifications affect **ribosome fidelity and splicing efficiency**, tightly linking RNA processing to ribosome performance. ", "keyword": "(\"SCARNA12\" OR \"SNORA68\") AND (\"RNA processing\" OR \"modifications\" OR \"ribosome\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": []}], "Cluster_RPLP0_3": [{"paragraph": "*SMUG1* is involved in **uracil-DNA glycosylation** but also plays a role in **RNA quality control**, especially during tRNA maturation. *WIBG* (PYM1) links **exon-junction complex (EJC) recycling** to translational activation and mRNA surveillance. *PDCD4* acts as a **translation inhibitor**, influencing the balance of protein synthesis and RNA turnover. ", "keyword": "(\"SMUG1\" OR \"PYM1\" OR \"PDCD4\") AND (\"uracil-DNA glycosylation\" OR \"RNA quality control\" OR \"translation inhibitor\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Krokan, Hans E, Drabl\u00f8s, Finn, Slupphaug, Geir. \"Uracil in DNA--occurrence, consequences and repair.\" Oncogene, 2002, pp. 8935-48, doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/sj.onc.1205996", "Jobert, Laure, Skjeldam, Hanne K, Dalhus, Bj\u00f8rn, Galashevskaya, Anastasia, V\u00e5gb\u00f8, Cathrine Broberg, Bj\u00f8r\u00e5s, Magnar, Nilsen, Hilde. \"The human base excision repair enzyme SMUG1 directly interacts with DKC1 and contributes to RNA quality control.\" Molecular cell, 2013, pp. 339-45, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molcel.2012.11.010", "Jobert, Laure, Nilsen, Hilde. \"Regulatory mechanisms of RNA function: emerging roles of DNA repair enzymes.\" Cellular and molecular life sciences : CMLS, 2014, pp. 2451-65, doi: https://doi.org/10.1007/s00018-014-1562-y"]}], "Cluster_RPLP0_4": [{"paragraph": "Several genes are involved in **mitochondrial protein synthesis and redox-linked translation**: -   *MRPS24* \u2013 mitochondrial small ribosomal subunit protein, key in mitochondrial translation. -   *FUNDC2, IMMP2L, COX14, ETHE1, MMAB, GPX7* \u2013 maintain **mitochondrial oxidative balance**, electron transport, and **cofactor biosynthesis**, indirectly modulating energy-dependent translation. This indicates a **functional bridge between mitochondrial and cytoplasmic translational activity**, possibly supporting dual-compartment protein synthesis coordination. ", "keyword": "(\"MRPS24\" OR \"FUNDC2\" OR \"IMMP2L\" OR \"COX14\" OR \"ETHE1\" OR \"MMAB\" OR \"GPX7\") AND (\"mitochondrial translation\" OR \"oxidative balance\" OR \"cofactor biosynthesis\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": []}], "Cluster_RPLP0_5": [{"paragraph": "Genes such as *VAMP8, RAB4A, TMEM14B, TMEM101, TMED3, AMFR* indicate **vesicular trafficking and ER-Golgi dynamics**, suggesting **translation-export coupling** for membrane or secretory proteins. This functional layer supports **co-translational translocation and protein quality assurance**. ", "keyword": "(\"VAMP8\" OR \"RAB4A\" OR \"TMEM14B\" OR \"TMEM101\" OR \"TMED3\" OR \"AMFR\") AND (\"vesicular trafficking\" OR \"ER-Golgi dynamics\" OR \"protein quality assurance\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": []}], "Cluster_RPLP0_6": [{"paragraph": "*ZNF16, ZNF22, ZNF32* encode **zinc finger proteins**, potentially linking transcriptional feedback with translation. *MGMT* and *HDDC3* contribute to **DNA repair and metabolic surveillance**, indirectly influencing mRNA stability and stress-induced translational arrest. ", "keyword": "(\"ZNF16\" OR \"ZNF22\" OR \"ZNF32\" OR \"MGMT\" OR \"HDDC3\") AND (\"transcription\" OR \"DNA repair\" OR \"metabolism\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Christmann, Markus, Kaina, Bernd. \"Epigenetic regulation of DNA repair genes and implications for tumor therapy.\" Mutation research. Reviews in mutation research, 2019, pp. 15-28, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mrrev.2017.10.001", "Bai, Peiying, Fan, Tengjiao, Sun, Guohui, Wang, Xin, Zhao, Lijiao, Zhong, Rugang. \"The dual role of DNA repair protein MGMT in cancer prevention and treatment.\" DNA repair, 2023, pp. 103449, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dnarep.2023.103449", "Peng, Yihan, Pei, Huadong. \"DNA alkylation lesion repair: outcomes and implications in cancer chemotherapy.\" Journal of Zhejiang University. Science. B, 2021, pp. 47-62, doi: https://doi.org/10.1631/jzus.B2000344"]}], "Cluster_SPEN_1": [{"paragraph": "This system prominently features **transcriptional regulators and chromatin modifiers**: -   *RBBP5, KDM5C, CHD2, ING5, TRRAP, ATRX, MED12, MED14, TADA2B, KAT8, NCOR1, UBN1, UBN2, PHC3, BCOR, WDR33* \u2013 involved in **histone modification, nucleosome remodeling, and transcriptional complex assembly**, critical for gene expression control. -   *WTAP* (a component of the m6A writer complex) links **epitranscriptomic regulation to transcriptional dynamics**. Together, these factors define a **chromatin-regulated transcriptional environment** that supports controlled RNA polymerase activity. ", "keyword": "(\"RBBP5\" OR \"KDM5C\" OR \"CHD2\" OR \"ING5\" OR \"TRRAP\" OR \"ATRX\" OR \"MED12\" OR \"MED14\" OR \"TADA2B\" OR \"KAT8\" OR \"NCOR1\" OR \"UBN1\" OR \"UBN2\" OR \"PHC3\" OR \"BCOR\" OR \"WDR33\" OR \"WTAP\") AND (\"transcriptional regulation\" OR \"chromatin modification\" OR \"gene expression\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Ping, Xiao-Li, Sun, Bao-Fa, Wang, Lu, Xiao, Wen, Yang, Xin, Wang, Wen-Jia, Adhikari, Samir, Shi, Yue, Lv, Ying, Chen, Yu-Sheng, Zhao, Xu, Li, Ang, Yang, Ying, Dahal, Ujwal, Lou, Xiao-Min, Liu, Xi, Huang, Jun, Yuan, Wei-Ping, Zhu, Xiao-Fan, Cheng, Tao, Zhao, Yong-Liang, Wang, Xinquan, Rendtlew Danielsen, Jannie M, Liu, Feng, Yang, Yun-Gui. \"Mammalian WTAP is a regulatory subunit of the RNA N6-methyladenosine methyltransferase.\" Cell research, 2014, pp. 177-89, doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/cr.2014.3", "Chen, Yunhao, Peng, Chuanhui, Chen, Junru, Chen, Diyu, Yang, Beng, He, Bin, Hu, Wendi, Zhang, Yanpeng, Liu, Hua, Dai, Longfei, Xie, Haiyang, Zhou, Lin, Wu, Jian, Zheng, Shusen. \"WTAP facilitates progression of hepatocellular carcinoma via m6A-HuR-dependent epigenetic silencing of ETS1.\" Molecular cancer, 2019, pp. 127, doi: https://doi.org/10.1186/s12943-019-1053-8", "Aguilera, Paula, L\u00f3pez-Contreras, Andr\u00e9s J. \"ATRX, a guardian of chromatin.\" Trends in genetics : TIG, 2023, pp. 505-519, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tig.2023.02.009"]}], "Cluster_SPEN_2": [{"paragraph": "Multiple proteins are involved in **RNA maturation and export coordination**: -   *PRPF8, RBM15, RBM27, AFF4, YTHDF1, LARP4* \u2013 function in **RNA binding, alternative splicing, and exon definition**. -   *NXF1, THOC2* \u2013 components of the **TREX/TAP export complex**, essential for **mRNA nuclear export**. -   *POM121, WTAP, ZCCHC6* \u2013 associate with **nuclear pore or RNA modification** complexes, coupling RNA surveillance to export readiness. This reflects a tight **coupling between transcription, splicing, and export** from the nucleus. ", "keyword": "(\"PRPF8\" OR \"RBM15\" OR \"RBM27\" OR \"AFF4\" OR \"YTHDF1\" OR \"LARP4\" OR \"NXF1\" OR \"THOC2\" OR \"POM121\" OR \"WTAP\" OR \"TUT7\") AND (\"RNA maturation\" OR \"mRNA export\" OR \"RNA binding\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Roundtree, Ian A, Luo, Guan-Zheng, Zhang, Zijie, Wang, Xiao, Zhou, Tao, Cui, Yiquang, Sha, Jiahao, Huang, Xingxu, Guerrero, Laura, Xie, Phil, He, Emily, Shen, Bin, He, Chuan. \"YTHDC1 mediates nuclear export of N<sup>6</sup>-methyladenosine methylated mRNAs.\" eLife, 2017, pp.  , doi: https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.31311"]}], "Cluster_SPEN_3": [{"paragraph": "-   *UBR4, UBR5, ITCH, HECTD1, HERC2, RNF111* \u2013 E3 ubiquitin ligases involved in **co-transcriptional protein turnover, chromatin-associated degradation**, and **modulation of transcriptional regulators**. -   *PSME4, CBL, UBE2O* \u2013 interface with **proteasome function**, contributing to **transcription-coupled degradation pathways**. These elements establish **quality control and transcriptional feedback** at the protein level. ", "keyword": "(\"UBR4\" OR \"UBR5\" OR \"ITCH\" OR \"HECTD1\" OR \"HERC2\" OR \"RNF111\" OR \"PSME4\" OR \"CBL\" OR \"UBE2O\") AND (\"protein turnover\" OR \"proteasome function\" OR \"transcriptional regulation\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Bolt, M J, Stossi, F, Callison, A M, Mancini, M G, Dandekar, R, Mancini, M A. \"Systems level-based RNAi screening by high content analysis identifies UBR5 as a regulator of estrogen receptor-\u03b1 protein levels and activity.\" Oncogene, 2015, pp. 154-64, doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/onc.2013.550"]}], "Cluster_SPEN_4": [{"paragraph": "-   *MTOR, MAP3K2, LATS1, PRKCD, TAOK3, PDPK1, ROCK2, SGK494* \u2013 kinases linking **signaling cascades to gene expression regulation**. -   These components enable **dynamic transcriptional responses to environmental or intracellular stimuli**, integrating metabolism, stress, and developmental inputs. ", "keyword": "(\"MTOR\" OR \"MAP3K2\" OR \"LATS1\" OR \"PRKCD\" OR \"TAOK3\" OR \"PDPK1\" OR \"ROCK2\" OR \"RSKR\") AND (\"signaling\" OR \"transcriptional regulation\" OR \"metabolism\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Sarbassov, D D, Guertin, David A, Ali, Siraj M, Sabatini, David M. \"Phosphorylation and regulation of Akt/PKB by the rictor-mTOR complex.\" Science (New York, N.Y.), 2005, pp. 1098-101, doi: https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1106148", "Saxton, Robert A, Sabatini, David M. \"mTOR Signaling in Growth, Metabolism, and Disease.\" Cell, 2017, pp. 960-976, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.02.004", "Gagliardi, Paolo Armando, Puliafito, Alberto, Primo, Luca. \"PDK1: At the crossroad of cancer signaling pathways.\" Seminars in cancer biology, 2018, pp. 27-35, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.semcancer.2017.04.014"]}], "Cluster_SPEN_5": [{"paragraph": "-   *CIZ1, PAPD5, ZFC3H1, RNF169* \u2013 contribute to **RNA stability, degradation of aberrant transcripts**, and **non-coding RNA regulation**. -   *WAC, PER2, HNRNPA1L2* \u2013 interface **transcriptional timing and circadian regulation** with RNA processing. ", "keyword": "(\"CIZ1\" OR \"TENT4B\" OR \"ZFC3H1\" OR \"RNF169\" OR \"WAC\" OR \"PER2\" OR \"HNRNPA1L2\") AND (\"RNA stability\" OR \"transcriptional timing\" OR \"circadian regulation\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Ogami, Koichi, Richard, Patricia, Chen, Yaqiong, Hoque, Mainul, Li, Wencheng, Moresco, James J, Yates, John R, Tian, Bin, Manley, James L. \"An Mtr4/ZFC3H1 complex facilitates turnover of unstable nuclear RNAs to prevent their cytoplasmic transport and global translational repression.\" Genes & development, 2017, pp. 1257-1271, doi: https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.302604.117", "Gery, S, Koeffler, H P. \"The role of circadian regulation in cancer.\" Cold Spring Harbor symposia on quantitative biology, 2007, pp. 459-64, doi: https://doi.org/10.1101/sqb.2007.72.004", "Wang, Yimin, Fan, Jing, Wang, Jianshu, Zhu, Yi, Xu, Lin, Tong, Deng, Cheng, Hong. \"ZFC3H1 prevents RNA trafficking into nuclear speckles through condensation.\" Nucleic acids research, 2021, pp. 10630-10643, doi: https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkab774"]}], "Cluster_SPEN_6": [{"paragraph": "-   *NUP-related proteins (POM121), TNPO2, ZNF106, KPNA1* \u2013 regulate **nucleocytoplasmic trafficking** and **nuclear scaffold dynamics**, ensuring the movement and localization of transcriptional machinery and mature RNAs. ", "keyword": "(\"POM121\" OR \"TNPO2\" OR \"ZNF106\" OR \"KPNA1\") AND (\"nucleocytoplasmic trafficking\" OR \"nuclear scaffold dynamics\" OR \"transcriptional machinery\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Jiang, Lucen, Li, Dan, Wang, Chao, Liao, Jia, Liu, Jianghuan, Wei, Qingzhu, Wang, Yiyang. \"Decreased Expression of Karyopherin-\u03b1 1 is Related to the Malignant Degree of Cervical Cancer and is Critical for the Proliferation of Hela Cells.\" Pathology oncology research : POR, 2022, pp. 1610518, doi: https://doi.org/10.3389/pore.2022.1610518"]}], "Cluster_PKM_1": [{"paragraph": "This system prominently features components regulated by or regulating **hypoxia-inducible factors (HIFs)**. *HIF1A*, *EGLN1*, *EGLN3*, *MIR210HG*, *VEGFA*, *BNIP3*, and *DDIT4* are core mediators of the transcriptional and metabolic response to low oxygen conditions. *EGLNs* hydroxylate HIF1A under normoxia, while *HIF1A* activates genes that enhance glycolytic flux, angiogenesis (*VEGFA*), and survival during hypoxic stress (*BNIP3*, *MIR210HG*). *DDIT4* connects hypoxia to mTOR inhibition, reducing energy expenditure. These factors establish a functional axis adapting metabolism and signaling to oxygen availability. ", "keyword": "(\"HIF1A\" OR \"EGLN1\" OR \"EGLN3\" OR \"VEGFA\" OR \"BNIP3\" OR \"DDIT4\") AND (\"hypoxia\" OR \"response\" OR \"metabolism\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Simonson, Tatum S, Yang, Yingzhong, Huff, Chad D, Yun, Haixia, Qin, Ga, Witherspoon, David J, Bai, Zhenzhong, Lorenzo, Felipe R, Xing, Jinchuan, Jorde, Lynn B, Prchal, Josef T, Ge, RiLi. \"Genetic evidence for high-altitude adaptation in Tibet.\" Science (New York, N.Y.), 2010, pp. 72-5, doi: https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1189406", "Li, Jialin, Lin, Qisheng, Shao, Xinghua, Li, Shu, Zhu, Xuying, Wu, Jingkui, Mou, Shan, Gu, Leyi, Wang, Qin, Zhang, Minfang, Zhang, Kaiqi, Lu, Jiayue, Ni, Zhaohui. \"HIF1\u03b1-BNIP3-mediated mitophagy protects against renal fibrosis by decreasing ROS and inhibiting activation of the NLRP3 inflammasome.\" Cell death & disease, 2023, pp. 200, doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41419-023-05587-5", "Lawson, Hannah, Holt-Martyn, James P, Dembitz, Vilma, Kabayama, Yuka, Wang, Lydia M, Bellani, Aarushi, Atwal, Samanpreet, Saffoon, Nadia, Durko, Jozef, van de Lagemaat, Louie N, De Pace, Azzura L, Tumber, Anthony, Corner, Thomas, Salah, Eidarus, Arndt, Christine, Brewitz, Lennart, Bowen, Matthew, Dubusse, Louis, George, Derek, Allen, Lewis, Guitart, Amelie V, Fung, Tsz Kan, So, Chi Wai Eric, Schwaller, Juerg, Gallipoli, Paolo, O'Carroll, Donal, Schofield, Christopher J, Kranc, Kamil R. \"The selective prolyl hydroxylase inhibitor IOX5 stabilizes HIF-1\u03b1 and compromises development and progression of acute myeloid leukemia.\" Nature cancer, 2024, pp. 916-937, doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/s43018-024-00761-w"]}], "Cluster_PKM_2": [{"paragraph": "Glycolytic genes including *PFKP*, *PFKL*, *ENO1*, *ENO2*, *ENO3*, *ALDOC*, *LDHA*, and *HK2* are key effectors of the hypoxia-induced metabolic shift. HIF1A upregulates these enzymes, favoring glycolysis and lactate production over mitochondrial respiration. This shift is supported by regulatory components like *PDK1*, *PDK3*, and *SLC16A3* (lactate transporter), which further suppress pyruvate entry into mitochondria and facilitate acid-base balance under anaerobic metabolism. ", "keyword": "(\"PFKP\" OR \"PFKL\" OR \"ENO1\" OR \"ENO2\" OR \"ENO3\" OR \"ALDOC\" OR \"LDHA\" OR \"HK2\" OR \"PDK1\" OR \"PDK3\" OR \"SLC16A3\") AND (\"glycolysis\" OR \"metabolic shift\" OR \"hypoxia\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Massari, Francesco, Ciccarese, Chiara, Santoni, Matteo, Iacovelli, Roberto, Mazzucchelli, Roberta, Piva, Francesco, Scarpelli, Marina, Berardi, Rossana, Tortora, Giampaolo, Lopez-Beltran, Antonio, Cheng, Liang, Montironi, Rodolfo. \"Metabolic phenotype of bladder cancer.\" Cancer treatment reviews, 2016, pp. 46-57, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ctrv.2016.03.005", "Cao, Lili, Wang, Min, Dong, Yujin, Xu, Bo, Chen, Ju, Ding, Yu, Qiu, Shusheng, Li, Liang, Karamfilova Zaharieva, Elena, Zhou, Xinwen, Xu, Yanbin. \"Circular RNA circRNF20 promotes breast cancer tumorigenesis and Warburg effect through miR-487a/HIF-1\u03b1/HK2.\" Cell death & disease, 2020, pp. 145, doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41419-020-2336-0", "Pouyss\u00e9gur, J, Marchiq, I, Parks, S K, Durivault, J, \u017ddralevi\u0107, M, Vucetic, M. \"'Warburg effect' controls tumor growth, bacterial, viral infections and immunity - Genetic deconstruction and therapeutic perspectives.\" Seminars in cancer biology, 2022, pp. 334-346, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.semcancer.2022.07.004"]}], "Cluster_PKM_3": [{"paragraph": "The system includes multiple integrins (*ITGB5*, *CD44*, *CD151*), ECM-modifying enzymes (*PLOD2*, *TIMP1*, *MMPs* indirectly via regulators like *TGFB1*), and cytoskeletal components (*VIM*, *ACTB*, *ACTN1*, *ARPC1B*, *ARPC2*, *ARPC4*, *CFL1*, *CAPG*). These genes support **cell adhesion dynamics, invasion, and motility**, which are often upregulated under hypoxia or during metastasis. *S100A4*, *S100A10*, and *VASP* contribute to lamellipodia and stress fiber formation. ", "keyword": "(\"ITGB5\" OR \"CD44\" OR \"CD151\" OR \"PLOD2\" OR \"TIMP1\" OR \"TGFB1\" OR \"VIM\" OR \"ACTB\" OR \"ACTN1\" OR \"ARPC1B\" OR \"ARPC2\" OR \"ARPC4\" OR \"CFL1\" OR \"CAPG\" OR \"S100A4\" OR \"S100A10\" OR \"VASP\") AND (\"cell adhesion\" OR \"metastasis\" OR \"motility\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Cheng, Zhongle, Wei, Wei, Wu, Zhengshen, Wang, Jing, Ding, Xiaojuan, Sheng, Youjing, Han, Yinli, Wu, Qiang. \"ARPC2 promotes breast cancer proliferation and metastasis.\" Oncology reports, 2019, pp. 3189-3200, doi: https://doi.org/10.3892/or.2019.7113", "Liu, Zhikui, Wang, Yufeng, Dou, Changwei, Xu, Meng, Sun, Liankang, Wang, Liang, Yao, Bowen, Li, Qing, Yang, Wei, Tu, Kangsheng, Liu, Qingguang. \"Hypoxia-induced up-regulation of VASP promotes invasiveness and metastasis of hepatocellular carcinoma.\" Theranostics, 2018, pp. 4649-4663, doi: https://doi.org/10.7150/thno.26789", "Kwiatkowski, Adam V, Gertler, Frank B, Loureiro, Joseph J. \"Function and regulation of Ena/VASP proteins.\" Trends in cell biology, 2003, pp. 386-92, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/s0962-8924(03)00130-2"]}], "Cluster_PKM_4": [{"paragraph": "Genes like *STX1A*, *NSF*, *ATP6V1A/B2*, *ATP6V0C*, *RAB7A*, and *VPS33B/18* regulate **endosome trafficking, acidification, and exocytosis**, crucial for receptor recycling, ECM component turnover, and autophagy under stress. These processes complement metabolic shifts by reallocating cellular resources and maintaining proteostasis. ", "keyword": "(\"STX1A\" OR \"NSF\" OR \"ATP6V1A\" OR \"ATP6V1B2\" OR \"ATP6V0C\" OR \"RAB7A\" OR \"VPS33B\" OR \"VPS18\") AND (\"endosome trafficking\" OR \"acidification\" OR \"exocytosis\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["S\u00fcdhof, Thomas C, Rizo, Josep. \"Synaptic vesicle exocytosis.\" Cold Spring Harbor perspectives in biology, 2011, pp.  , doi: https://doi.org/10.1101/cshperspect.a005637", "Morgan, A. \"Exocytosis.\" Essays in biochemistry, 1995, pp. 77-95.", "Ren, Xiang, Wang, Jing, Wei, Huizhi, Li, Xing, Tian, Yiqun, Wang, Zhixian, Yin, Yisheng, Guo, Zihao, Qin, Zhenliang, Wu, Minglong, Zeng, Xiaoyong. \"Impaired TFEB-mediated autophagy-lysosome fusion promotes tubular cell cycle G2/M arrest and renal fibrosis by suppressing ATP6V0C expression and interacting with SNAREs.\" International journal of biological sciences, 2024, pp. 1905-1926, doi: https://doi.org/10.7150/ijbs.91480"]}], "Cluster_PKM_5": [{"paragraph": "While glycolysis is enhanced, mitochondrial support genes like *UQCRC1*, *COX5A*, *COX6B1*, *MRPS6/34*, *GLS*, *ETFA*, and *MICU1* indicate **ongoing mitochondrial activity and redox regulation**. *GPX4* and *NQO1* help prevent oxidative stress, a frequent consequence of hypoxia and altered metabolism. ", "keyword": "(\"UQCRC1\" OR \"COX5A\" OR \"COX6B1\" OR \"MRPS6\" OR \"GLS\" OR \"ETFA\" OR \"MICU1\" OR \"GPX4\" OR \"NQO1\") AND (\"mitochondrial activity\" OR \"redox regulation\" OR \"oxidative stress\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Ross, David, Siegel, David. \"The diverse functionality of NQO1 and its roles in redox control.\" Redox biology, 2021, pp. 101950, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.redox.2021.101950", "Zhang, Peipei, Lu, Hao, Wu, Yuan, Lu, Danbo, Li, Chenguang, Yang, Xiangdong, Chen, Zhangwei, Qian, Juying, Ge, Junbo. \"COX5A Alleviates Doxorubicin-Induced Cardiotoxicity by Suppressing Oxidative Stress, Mitochondrial Dysfunction and Cardiomyocyte Apoptosis.\" International journal of molecular sciences, 2023, pp.  , doi: https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms241210400"]}], "Cluster_PKM_6": [{"paragraph": "Numerous transcriptional regulators (*SMAD3*, *MEF2A*, *RBPJ*, *ARNTL2*, *HDAC1*, *SIN3A*, *NRD1*, *NONO*, *SLTM*) coordinate the expression of hypoxia-responsive, metabolic, and cytoskeletal genes. *BHLHE40*, induced by hypoxia, participates in circadian and stress-adaptive gene programs. Chromatin remodelers (*EHMT2*, *LEO1*) fine-tune gene expression patterns under shifting environmental conditions. ", "keyword": "(\"SMAD3\" OR \"MEF2A\" OR \"RBPJ\" OR \"BMAL2\" OR \"HDAC1\" OR \"SIN3A\" OR \"NRDC\" OR \"NONO\" OR \"SLTM\" OR \"BHLHE40\" OR \"EHMT2\" OR \"LEO1\") AND (\"transcriptional regulation\" OR \"hypoxia\" OR \"response\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": []}], "Cluster_AKAP8_1": [{"paragraph": "This system includes multiple components of the circadian clock (*PER2, PER3, CRY2, NR1D1*), which regulate daily oscillations of gene expression in metabolic tissues. These transcriptional regulators control the rhythmic expression of key metabolic enzymes and transporters, thereby orchestrating the timing of energy storage, mobilization, and hormonal signaling across the light-dark cycle. Their co-presence with nutrient transporters and signaling proteins suggests functional integration in time-dependent metabolic homeostasis. ", "keyword": "(\"PER2\" OR \"PER3\" OR \"CRY2\" OR \"NR1D1\") AND (\"circadian\" OR \"metabolic\" OR \"homeostasis\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Miro, Caterina, Docimo, Annamaria, Barrea, Luigi, Verde, Ludovica, Cernea, Simona, Sojat, Antoan Stefan, Marina, Ljiljana V, Docimo, Giovanni, Colao, Annamaria, Dentice, Monica, Muscogiuri, Giovanna. \"\"Time\" for obesity-related cancer: The role of the circadian rhythm in cancer pathogenesis and treatment.\" Seminars in cancer biology, 2023, pp. 99-109, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.semcancer.2023.03.003", "Liu, Zhihua, Chu, Guiyan. \"Chronobiology in mammalian health.\" Molecular biology reports, 2013, pp. 2491-501, doi: https://doi.org/10.1007/s11033-012-2330-4", "Levine, Daniel C, Hong, Heekyung, Weidemann, Benjamin J, Ramsey, Kathryn M, Affinati, Alison H, Schmidt, Mark S, Cedernaes, Jonathan, Omura, Chiaki, Braun, Rosemary, Lee, Choogon, Brenner, Charles, Peek, Clara Bien, Bass, Joseph. \"NAD<sup>+</sup> Controls Circadian Reprogramming through PER2 Nuclear Translocation to Counter Aging.\" Molecular cell, 2020, pp. 835-849.e7, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molcel.2020.04.010"]}], "Cluster_AKAP8_2": [{"paragraph": "Key metabolic effectors such as *INSR* (insulin receptor), *SLC2A4* (GLUT4), and *ADCY5* (adenylate cyclase 5) are central to insulin-stimulated glucose uptake in skeletal muscle and adipose tissue. *SLC2A4* translocates to the membrane in response to insulin signaling via *INSR*, facilitating glucose entry into cells. *ADCY5* contributes to cAMP-mediated modulation of insulin secretion and signaling. These proteins form a coordinated module that transduces insulin signals to regulate glucose utilization, strongly linking this system to energy metabolism. ", "keyword": "(\"INSR\" OR \"SLC2A4\" OR \"ADCY5\") AND (\"glucose uptake\" OR \"insulin signaling\" OR \"energy metabolism\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["H\u00f8jlund, Kurt. \"Metabolism and insulin signaling in common metabolic disorders and inherited insulin resistance.\" Danish medical journal, 2014, pp. B4890."]}], "Cluster_AKAP8_3": [{"paragraph": "Genes like *FAAH* (fatty acid amide hydrolase), *DAGLA* (diacylglycerol lipase alpha), *DGKD* (diacylglycerol kinase delta), *SREBF1* (a transcriptional regulator of lipid biosynthesis), and *COQ10A* (coenzyme Q10 biosynthesis) contribute to lipid signaling and storage. Their integration suggests the system supports lipid flux coordination, particularly in metabolically active tissues where insulin and circadian signals converge. ", "keyword": "(\"FAAH\" OR \"DAGLA\" OR \"DGKD\" OR \"SREBF1\" OR \"COQ10A\") AND (\"lipid signaling\" OR \"lipid biosynthesis\" OR \"metabolic regulation\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Steen, Vidar M, Skrede, Silje, Polushina, Tatiana, L\u00f3pez, Miguel, Andreassen, Ole A, Fern\u00f8, Johan, Hellard, Stephanie Le. \"Genetic evidence for a role of the SREBP transcription system and lipid biosynthesis in schizophrenia and antipsychotic treatment.\" European neuropsychopharmacology : the journal of the European College of Neuropsychopharmacology, 2017, pp. 589-598, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.euroneuro.2016.07.011"]}], "Cluster_AKAP8_4": [{"paragraph": "Solute carrier proteins (*SLC22A5, SLC45A3, SLC46A1*) and enzymes like *L2HGDH* and *CKMT2* indicate participation in mitochondrial metabolism and organic solute transport. These molecules sustain energy production by managing the import and export of critical cofactors, such as carnitine (*SLC22A5*), which is essential for fatty acid \u03b2-oxidation. *CKMT2* couples ATP production to energy-demanding processes in tissues like heart and muscle. ", "keyword": "(\"SLC22A5\" OR \"SLC45A3\" OR \"SLC46A1\" OR \"L2HGDH\" OR \"CKMT2\") AND (\"mitochondrial metabolism\" OR \"organic solute transport\" OR \"energy production\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["M\u00fcller, Sebastian, Balaz, Miroslav, Stefanicka, Patrik, Varga, Lukas, Amri, Ez-Zoubir, Ukropec, Jozef, Wollscheid, Bernd, Wolfrum, Christian. \"Proteomic Analysis of Human Brown Adipose Tissue Reveals Utilization of Coupled and Uncoupled Energy Expenditure Pathways.\" Scientific reports, 2016, pp. 30030, doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/srep30030"]}], "Cluster_AKAP8_5": [{"paragraph": "*DEPTOR*, a regulator of mTOR signaling, functions as a metabolic rheostat under nutrient availability and insulin conditions. Trafficking proteins like *HOOK2, GGA3*, and *PITPNM2* contribute to endosomal sorting and membrane dynamics, processes essential for glucose transporter recycling and hormonal signal propagation. These components ensure that signaling and nutrient uptake are tightly coupled with membrane trafficking pathways. ", "keyword": "(\"DEPTOR\" OR \"HOOK2\" OR \"GGA3\" OR \"PITPNM2\") AND (\"mTOR signaling\" OR \"metabolic regulation\" OR \"membrane trafficking\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": []}], "Cluster_AKAP8_6": [{"paragraph": "Proteins like *JAG1* (a Notch ligand) and *LRP5* (a Wnt co-receptor involved in metabolic tissue homeostasis) suggest developmental regulation of metabolic tissue architecture and function. *AMIGO1* and *PLEKHA7* also influence cellular structure and junctional stability, potentially affecting tissue responsiveness to hormonal and circadian cues. ", "keyword": "(\"JAG1\" OR \"LRP5\" OR \"AMIGO1\" OR \"PLEKHA7\") AND (\"developmental regulation\" OR \"metabolic tissue\" OR \"cellular structure\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": []}], "Cluster_PAX5_1": [{"paragraph": "Multiple immunoglobulin variable genes (e.g., *IGHV*, *IGLV*, *IGKV*, *IGLJ*, *IGHM*) are represented, indicating a system centered on **B-cell receptor diversification and clonal selection**. Accompanying these are genes like *CD79A* and *MS4A1* (CD20), which are critical for B-cell receptor (BCR) signaling and maturation. *T-cell signaling* is also prominently featured, as indicated by *CD80*, *LAT*, *LAT2*, *LCK*, *TRAV19*, *TRBV20OR9-2*, and *PDCD1*. These genes mediate TCR signal transduction, co-stimulation, and T-cell exhaustion or tolerance. The co-presence of both B-cell and T-cell lineage-specific components suggests this system supports **bidirectional crosstalk and co-regulation between adaptive immune arms**. ", "keyword": "(\"LOC102723407\" OR \"IGLL5\" OR \"IGKV1-5\" OR \"IGLJ\" OR \"IGHM\" OR \"CD79A\" OR \"MS4A1\" OR \"CD80\" OR \"LAT\" OR \"LAT2\" OR \"LCK\" OR \"TRAV19\" OR \"TRBV20OR9-2\" OR \"PDCD1\") AND (\"immune system\" OR \"signal transduction\" OR \"adaptive immunity\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Courtney, Adam H, Lo, Wan-Lin, Weiss, Arthur. \"TCR Signaling: Mechanisms of Initiation and Propagation.\" Trends in biochemical sciences, 2018, pp. 108-123, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tibs.2017.11.008", "Fischer, S, Marie-Cardine, A, Ramos-Morales, F, Bougeret, C, Soula, M, Maridonneau-Parini, I, Benarous, R. \"P56lck A lymphocyte specific protein tyrosine kinase: activation, regulation and signal transduction.\" Cellular and molecular biology (Noisy-le-Grand, France), 1994, pp. 605-9."]}], "Cluster_PAX5_2": [{"paragraph": "Genes such as *IL10RA*, *IL21R*, *IFNA2*, *TNF*, *IL32*, *CCL22*, *CCR5*, and *CXCR5* encode cytokines, receptors, or chemokines directly involved in immune cell recruitment, proliferation, or polarization. Their concerted expression indicates **a regulatory network governing cytokine-mediated responses**, including Th1/Th2 skewing, inflammation, and immune cell trafficking. This is complemented by transcriptional regulators such as *IRF4*, *SPIB*, and *SKIL*, which shape the expression of cytokine receptors and immunoregulatory genes. ", "keyword": "(\"IL10RA\" OR \"IL21R\" OR \"IFNA2\" OR \"TNF\" OR \"IL32\" OR \"CCL22\" OR \"CCR5\" OR \"CXCR5\") AND (\"cytokine-mediated responses\" OR \"immune cell recruitment\" OR \"regulatory network\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Su, Fei, Zhang, Wei, Meng, Lingfeng, Zhang, Wei, Liu, Xiaodong, Liu, Xiaorui, Chen, Meng, Zhang, Yaoguang, Xiao, Fei. \"Multimodal Single-Cell Analyses Outline the Immune Microenvironment and Therapeutic Effectors of Interstitial Cystitis/Bladder Pain Syndrome.\" Advanced science (Weinheim, Baden-Wurttemberg, Germany), 2022, pp. e2106063, doi: https://doi.org/10.1002/advs.202106063"]}], "Cluster_PAX5_3": [{"paragraph": "Downstream signaling components such as *CARD11*, *PIK3R5*, *RASGRP2*, *DYRK1B*, and *TRIM61* integrate antigen receptor stimulation into transcriptional programs. These effectors interface with the NF-\u03baB and MAPK pathways, promoting immune cell activation, proliferation, and survival. Effector molecules such as *GNLY* (granulysin) and *NKG7* highlight the cytotoxic arm of lymphocyte function, suggesting that this network extends into **cell-mediated cytotoxicity**. ", "keyword": "(\"CARD11\" OR \"PIK3R5\" OR \"RASGRP2\" OR \"DYRK1B\" OR \"TRIM61\" OR \"GNLY\" OR \"NKG7\") AND (\"immune activation\" OR \"cell-mediated cytotoxicity\" OR \"signaling pathways\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": []}], "Cluster_PAX5_4": [{"paragraph": "Several long non-coding RNAs (e.g., *MIR17HG*, *IFNG-AS1*, *H19*, *RAD51-AS1*, *JARID2-AS1*) and small RNAs (*MIR142*, *MIR3916*, *SNORA1*, *SNORA73*) are known to regulate transcriptional activity, splicing, and translation in immune contexts. For example, *MIR17HG* and *IFNG-AS1* are involved in **T-cell polarization and cytokine regulation**. Y\\_RNAs and RN7SK pseudogenes suggest modulation of RNA stability and chromatin remodeling, potentially linking transcriptional burst control to immune activation. ", "keyword": "(\"MIR17HG\" OR \"IFNG-AS1\" OR \"H19\" OR \"RAD51-AS1\" OR \"JARID2-AS1\" OR \"MIR142\" OR \"MIR3916\" OR \"SNORA1\" OR \"SNORA73\") AND (\"transcriptional regulation\" OR \"immune activation\" OR \"RNA stability\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Al-Raawi, Diaa, Kanhere, Aditi. \"Autoregulation of JARID2 through PRC2 interaction with its antisense ncRNA.\" BMC research notes, 2020, pp. 501, doi: https://doi.org/10.1186/s13104-020-05348-z"]}], "Cluster_PAX5_5": [{"paragraph": "Other associated genes (*ZBP1*, *TICAM2*, *TLR9*) point toward **innate immune sensors and signaling pathways**, suggesting this system may serve as a bridge between **innate and adaptive immunity**. Furthermore, the presence of MHC-related genes such as *HLA-DRB1* and *HLA-DQB1-AS1* supports antigen processing and presentation, a key function at the interface of innate sensing and adaptive activation. ", "keyword": "(\"ZBP1\" OR \"TICAM2\" OR \"TLR9\" OR \"HLA-DRB1\" OR \"HLA-DQB1-AS1\") AND (\"innate immunity\" OR \"antigen processing\" OR \"adaptive immunity\") AND (hasabstract[text]) AND humans[mh] NOT Retracted Publication[pt]", "references": ["Riley, Joel S, Tait, Stephen Wg. \"Mitochondrial DNA in inflammation and immunity.\" EMBO reports, 2020, pp. e49799, doi: https://doi.org/10.15252/embr.201949799", "Malireddi, R K Subbarao, Kesavardhana, Sannula, Kanneganti, Thirumala-Devi. \"ZBP1 and TAK1: Master Regulators of NLRP3 Inflammasome/Pyroptosis, Apoptosis, and Necroptosis (PAN-optosis).\" Frontiers in cellular and infection microbiology, 2019, pp. 406, doi: https://doi.org/10.3389/fcimb.2019.00406", "Lee, SangJoon, Karki, Rajendra, Wang, Yaqiu, Nguyen, Lam Nhat, Kalathur, Ravi C, Kanneganti, Thirumala-Devi. \"AIM2 forms a complex with pyrin and ZBP1 to drive PANoptosis and host defence.\" Nature, 2021, pp. 415-419, doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-021-03875-8"]}]}